course: dictionary
lesson: 4980
title: Indeed: really, yes, or in fact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indeed is a small word with several jobs. Most often it makes something stronger, like «really» or «truly»: «Thank you very much indeed.» It can also mean «yes, that is true», as in «"It's cold." "Indeed it is."»
explain: Indeed can add a stronger point. In persuasive writing it links one idea to a bigger one: «Pets are good for us; indeed, they can help us feel calmer.» Here indeed means «in fact», so the second idea goes further than the first.
explain: To find the right meaning, look at the context. If indeed answers or agrees with what someone just said, it means yes. If it sits inside a sentence and makes a describing word stronger, it means really. Try swapping in «really» or «in fact» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Indeed is an adverb.
fact: «Indeed» means «really» or «truly» when it makes something stronger, as in «very good indeed».
fact: «Indeed» means «yes, that is true» when it agrees with someone.
fact: «Indeed» means «in fact» when it adds a stronger point, and it is often used in formal writing.
fact: In everyday speech indeed sounds a little formal or old-fashioned, so you will often meet it in stories, speeches and persuasive writing.
exercise: «He was indeed an altered Toad!» What does indeed mean here? | He was not an altered Toad | Quietly, under his breath | Slowly, one step at a time | *Really, he was truly changed
exercise: Toad says, «I'm a nuisance, I know.» The Rat replies, «You are, indeed.» What does the Rat mean? | Please stop talking now | You are a frog, not a toad | No, you are not a nuisance | *Yes, that is true, you are a nuisance
exercise: On Easter Sunday, one friend says, «Christ is risen!» The other replies, «He is risen indeed!» What does indeed mean in the reply? | *Yes, it is truly so | Maybe, we will see | Goodbye until next year | He is not risen at all
test: «The end was indeed nearer than even the Rat suspected.» What does indeed do in this sentence? | *It makes nearer stronger, meaning the end was really closer | It says goodbye to the Rat | It says the end was far away | It asks a question about the end
test: «Pets are good for us; indeed, they can help us feel calmer.» What does indeed add here? | *A stronger point, meaning in fact | A sad feeling about pets | A question about pets | A reason to stop reading
exam: Which reply uses indeed to agree with "It's cold."? | Goodbye, indeed | *Indeed it is | Indeed, it is a cake | No, it is warm
